Now tutorial hint and maybe foreground grass. Let's add hint in onLevelStart:
```js
if (index===0) {
 clearTimeout(hintTimer);
 hintTimer=setTimeout(()=>{ if(game.mode==='play' && game.levelIndex===0 && game.collectedCount===0) showToast('hold jump to float · press again in the air to double-jump') }, 3600);
}
```
But if fresh start, fine. If user idles, appears. If they already moved/collected, no. Add hintTimer var.

Also maybe on level 5 gate, toast handles.

Foreground grass: add method and call. Let's think if needed. The bottom dirt is a large blank area in desktop gameplay and mobile. Adding foreground plant silhouettes at the bottom could improve depth. We can draw 18 blades screen-space rooted at h+10 across width, using theme.foregroundColor with alpha .2, sway. But the ground block already there; blades would look like grass at the very bottom close to camera, which is natural. They would be static relative to screen horizontally except subtle parallax? Keep screen-space fixed with slight sway. Add 14 tufts at seeded x, heights 30-80, alpha .18, blur? Canvas no blur (expensive). Simple filled shapes with dark green. Also a soft rounded leaf at bottom corners. Could frame nicely and hide the emptiness. Add after world before weather. Don't draw on complete/pause? Render always, so on menus too; fine.

Implementation:
```js
_drawForeground(ctx,w,h) {
 const th=this.levelDef.theme;
 ctx.save();
 ctx.globalAlpha=0.35;
 ctx.fillStyle=th.foregroundColor;
 for i 0..15: x = ((i*137)%w)+...; baseY=h+14; hh=30+hash(i)*50; sway=...
   draw 3 blades per tuft
 ctx.restore();
}
```
This might cover the player when at bottom? Player never at screen bottom; camera keeps player ~56% height. Fine. It might overlap mobile touch buttons but they are DOM above. Good.

Add a soft top gradient? No.

Also add a vignette bottom darkening via existing radial.

Let's add both.

Also one more important gameplay thing: level restart from pause resets stars, but the save's stars for that level clear; okay.

The pause overlay has "restart level" and "back to meadow" as good.

Tutorial hints and level intro card: check later.

Now add foreground and hint.

