Whoa, fallTimer stuck at 0.97 and y=1365. It should decrement in `_step` only when `this.fallTimer > 0`; but `_frame` skips stepping when `this.fallTimer > 0`? Let's check:

```
if (this.mode === 'play' && this.fallTimer <= 0) {
  this.accum += dt; step...
}
if (mode paused/complete) accum = 0;
...
```

So when fallTimer > 0, `_step` is never called! In `_step`, fallTimer decrement occurs, but `_frame` refuses to call `_step` when fallTimer > 0. That's a bug: fall timer never decrements, and player never respawns! Wait, how did playtest see fall? It calls `g._step(1/120)` directly, bypassing `_frame`. Also `_frame` calls `_updateVisuals` when fallTimer>0, but not `_step`. So in actual gameplay, falling into a pit results in permanent freeze at y=1365 with fallTimer 0.97. That's a significant bug.

Let's examine `_frame` lines 308: condition `this.mode === 'play' && this.fallTimer <= 0`. It likely was intended to stop physics when falling (so input ignored) but then no one updates fallTimer. Maybe elsewhere fallTimer decremented in visuals? No. So yes, bug. Fix: allow stepping when fallTimer > 0, because _step handles fallTimer and early returns. Remove `&& this.fallTimer <= 0`. But then `_step` still calls `_updateMovers` before fall handling and skips player/pickups. That's fine. Or decrement fallTimer in frame separately. Cleaner: in `_frame`, always accumulate when mode play, and `_step` handles fall. Let's check fall detection in `_updatePlayer`.

